Synopsis: My research integrates biology, biopolymer science, and cement chemistry to create biomimetic, carbon-storing, and engineered living material technologies. To date, I have served as PI for sponsored research projects totaling >$14.5M, of which I received >$9.8 M. I have served as co-PI for sponsored research projects totaling >$13.2M, of which I received >$2.2M. I have published >100 peer-reviewed technical journal articles, book chapters, and conference proceedings, and I hold two US patents. I have seven patents that are currently pending. As of 1 January 2025, I have a Google Scholar H-Index: 31. I teach courses in materials science, mechanics, sustainability, and structural engineering.
